order of severity. No ports: each page is a real OneShot, Vault or Home
whose socket is never bound, and every request goes over a
socket.socketpair() straight into the server's own finish_request, so the
real handler reads the real bytes. `tailscale serve status` is patched to show
the page's route; `security` is the fake in tests/fakes.py.

    tests/keydrop-review-test

KEYDROP_UNDER_TEST=<path> runs the same tests against another copy of the
script (an older commit, say), to see which of them it fails.
"""
